## 1. Curl test — każdy header ręcznie

```bash
DOMAIN="{{PROD_DOMAIN}}"

# Pobierz wszystkie headers i zapisz do pliku
curl -sI "https://${DOMAIN}" > /tmp/headers.txt
cat /tmp/headers.txt
```

### Weryfikacja każdego headera (expect: wszystkie PASS)

```bash
DOMAIN="{{PROD_DOMAIN}}"

# HSTS
echo "--- HSTS ---"
curl -sI "https://${DOMAIN}" | grep -i "strict-transport"
# Oczekiwane: Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload

# X-Frame-Options
echo "--- X-Frame-Options ---"
curl -sI "https://${DOMAIN}" | grep -i "x-frame"
# Oczekiwane: X-Frame-Options: DENY

# X-Content-Type-Options
echo "--- X-Content-Type-Options ---"
curl -sI "https://${DOMAIN}" | grep -i "x-content-type"
# Oczekiwane: X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff

# Referrer-Policy
echo "--- Referrer-Policy ---"
curl -sI "https://${DOMAIN}" | grep -i "referrer"
# Oczekiwane: Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# Permissions-Policy
echo "--- Permissions-Policy ---"
curl -sI "https://${DOMAIN}" | grep -i "permissions"
# Oczekiwane: Permissions-Policy: camera=, microphone=, geolocation=, ...

# CSP
echo "--- Content-Security-Policy ---"
curl -sI "https://${DOMAIN}" | grep -i "content-security"
# Oczekiwane: Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'nonce-...' 'strict-dynamic'; ...

# Sprawdź czy NIE ma 'unsafe-eval' w CSP produkcji
echo "--- CSP unsafe-eval check (should be empty) ---"
curl -sI "https://${DOMAIN}" | grep -i "content-security" | grep "unsafe-eval"
# Oczekiwane: PUSTA linia (unsafe-eval NIE powinna być w produkcji)

# Sprawdź brak Server header (ukryte przez Caddy)
echo "--- Server header (should be empty) ---"
curl -sI "https://${DOMAIN}" | grep -i "^server:"
# Oczekiwane: PUSTA linia (Caddy usuwa Server header)
```

